<details class="plan-chapter" id="project-detail-3"><summary><span class="chapter-count">03</span><h3>Landscape Installation Services in Brighton, CO — Done Right From the Ground Up</h3>
<span aria-hidden="true" class="chapter-toggle">+</span></summary><div class="chapter-body prose"><p>Getting landscape installation right in Brighton starts well before the first plant goes in the ground. Brighton’s alkaline, clay-heavy soils require genuine preparation — not just clearing and planting. Without proper soil amendment, drainage work, and grading, even the right plants in the right positions struggle to establish. And hardscape elements installed without accounting for Brighton’s ground movement through winter freeze-thaw cycles develop problems within a few seasons that are expensive to correct.</p>
<p>Our installation teams have been working in Adams County and the northern Denver metro since 2011. We assess soil conditions before specifying amendments. We design grading and drainage into the project from the outset — not as an afterthought when standing water appears. We install irrigation systems that account for Brighton’s evaporation rates and the city’s watering guidelines. Every installation decision is made with the site’s actual conditions in mind.</p>
<p>We handle the full landscape installation scope in-house: site grading and drainage, soil preparation and amendment, irrigation system design and installation, turf establishment (sod or seed), planting bed preparation and planting, hardscape integration, and final site cleanup. No phase is handed off to a subcontractor. The team that designs the landscape is the team that builds it — which means nothing gets lost in translation between the plan and the finished result.</p>

<h3>Garden Landscaping Services in Brighton Designed for Colorado's Climate
</h3>

<p>Brighton homeowners increasingly want landscapes that go beyond lawn and a few foundation shrubs — garden landscapes with structure, seasonal interest, and planting that feels designed rather than assembled. The challenge in Colorado is designing a garden landscape that looks intentional and holds up through conditions that aren’t forgiving of poorly chosen plants or layouts that don’t account for the site’s realities.</p>
<p>Our garden landscaping services in Brighton start with understanding what you want the space to feel like and how you’ll use it — then designing a planting scheme and layout that can actually deliver that through Colorado’s growing season. That means plant selections based on proven Colorado performance: drought-tolerant perennials that return reliably, shrubs that handle hard winters without significant dieback, native and adapted plants that work with Brighton’s soil and water conditions rather than against them.</p>
<p>We design garden landscapes for both front yards and backyards — kerb appeal plantings that give a Brighton property a distinctive, polished look through the season, and backyard garden designs that create defined spaces for relaxing, entertaining, or growing. Garden landscapes are also a smart water-management tool in Colorado: well-chosen, well-placed planting in mulched beds significantly reduces irrigation demand compared to high-maintenance turf.</p>
<p>Every garden landscape we design comes with a planting plan that specifies each species, its position, and its relationship to the other elements in the design — so the installation delivers exactly what the design intended.</p>
</div>
</details>
<details class="plan-chapter" id="project-detail-4"><summary><span class="chapter-count">04</span><h3>Commercial Landscape Service in Brighton for Properties That Make the Right Impression</h3>
<span aria-hidden="true" class="chapter-toggle">+</span></summary><div class="chapter-body prose"><p>Brighton’s commercial landscape has grown significantly as the city has expanded — new retail, office, and mixed-use development alongside established business parks and commercial corridors that need their landscape to project professionalism and attract customers. For commercial properties in Brighton, the landscape is part of the business presentation. It’s one of the first things customers, tenants, and partners see, and it communicates something about the quality of what’s inside before anyone walks through the door.</p>
<p>Ridgewell provides commercial landscape services in Brighton for businesses, property managers, HOAs, and commercial developers. Our commercial work covers the full design and installation scope — creating landscapes that are professionally designed, properly built, and specified to be manageable long-term without demanding excessive maintenance resources from your property team.</p>
<p>We design commercial landscapes around the realities of commercial property operation in Brighton. Plant selections are chosen for durability and low ongoing maintenance. Irrigation systems are zoned efficiently and specified to minimise adjustment. Hardscape elements — entry treatments, pathways, defined planting zones, feature areas — are built for long-term appearance and high foot traffic, not just how they look at handover.</p>
<p>Brighton’s commercial landscape projects often involve new construction timelines, stakeholder sign-off requirements, and site access constraints during active business operations. Our process is structured for all of it — clear scoping upfront, direct communication throughout, and installation scheduled to minimise disruption to your business and your customers.</p>
</div>
</details>
