<details class="plan-chapter" id="project-detail-8"><summary><span class="chapter-count">08</span><h3>What Brighton Homeowners and Business Owners Ask Us Most About Landscape Services</h3>
<span aria-hidden="true" class="chapter-toggle">+</span></summary><div class="chapter-body prose"><div class="content-feature">
<div id="eael-adv-accordion-c132f7d">
<div id="what-landscape-services-does-ridgewell-offer-in-brighton-co"><h3>What landscape services does Ridgewell offer in Brighton, CO?</h3>
</div>
<div id="elementor-tab-content-2021"><p>We provide full-service landscape design and installation in Brighton, CO, covering residential and commercial projects. Our Brighton landscape services include: custom landscape design, lawn installation (sod and seed), garden landscape design and planting, planting bed establishment, irrigation system design and installation, xeriscaping and water-wise landscaping, hardscape integration (patios, pathways, retaining walls), site grading and drainage, and commercial landscape design and installation. Every project is handled as a complete scope — design through to finished installation — by our in-house team.</p>
</div>

<div id="how-much-do-landscaping-services-cost-in-brighton-co-"><h3>How much do landscaping services cost in Brighton, CO? </h3>
</div>
<div id="elementor-tab-content-2022"><p>Brighton landscape project costs vary based on property size, scope, and the combination of services involved. A front yard redesign with new planting, lawn, and edging typically starts around $5,000–$10,000. A full backyard landscape installation with irrigation, hardscape, and comprehensive planting generally ranges from $15,000–$40,000. Garden landscape designs and commercial installations vary depending on scope and site complexity. We provide detailed, itemised quotes after an in-person site assessment — so you have a clear and accurate picture of costs before committing to the project.</p>
</div>

<div id="do-you-offer-garden-landscaping-services-in-brighton"><h3>Do you offer garden landscaping services in Brighton?</h3>
</div>
<div id="elementor-tab-content-2023"><p>Yes. Garden landscaping is one of our core residential services in Brighton. We design and install garden landscapes that go beyond standard lawn-and-shrub setups — planting schemes with structure, seasonal interest, and species chosen for proven performance in Colorado’s climate. Our garden landscaping work covers front yard kerb appeal designs, backyard garden installations, and mixed landscape projects that combine garden planting with lawn, hardscape, and outdoor living elements. Every garden landscape comes with a detailed planting plan so the installation delivers exactly what the design intended.</p>
</div>

<div id="-do-you-provide-commercial-landscape-services-in-brighton-"><h3> Do you provide commercial landscape services in Brighton? </h3>
</div>
<div id="elementor-tab-content-2024"><p>Yes. We provide commercial landscape design and installation for businesses, property managers, HOAs, and commercial developers in Brighton. Our commercial landscape service covers the full design and build scope — plant selections chosen for durability and low maintenance, efficient irrigation systems, and hardscape elements built for long-term commercial use. We work with commercial clients on Brighton’s new construction timelines and active-site constraints, and our process is structured to minimise disruption to business operations during installation</p>
</div>

<div id="how-does-your-colorado-lawn-and-landscape-service-approach-brightons-soil-conditions"><h3>How does your Colorado lawn and landscape service approach Brighton's soil conditions?</h3>
</div>
<div id="elementor-tab-content-2025"><p>Brighton’s soils are typically alkaline and clay-heavy — conditions that present real challenges for landscape establishment if they’re not addressed properly at the installation stage. Our process includes a soil assessment before specifying amendments, proper drainage design to manage Brighton’s water retention issues, and plant selections chosen for performance in these specific soil conditions. We amend soil where needed before planting, not after problems appear. This upfront work is what makes the difference between a landscape that establishes well and one that struggles in its first season.</p>
</div>

<div id="how-long-does-landscape-installation-take-in-brighton-"><h3>How long does landscape installation take in Brighton? </h3>
</div>
<div id="elementor-tab-content-2026"><p> Project timelines in Brighton depend on scope. A front yard refresh with new planting, sod, and edging can be completed in a few days. A full backyard landscape installation with irrigation, hardscape, and comprehensive planting typically takes 2–4 weeks. Commercial projects and full property transformations take longer depending on scale and site conditions. We provide a detailed project schedule before work starts and keep you informed throughout so there are no surprises about timing.</p>
</div>

<div id="can-you-handle-both-the-lawn-and-garden-elements-of-a-brighton-landscape-project-"><h3>Can you handle both the lawn and garden elements of a Brighton landscape project? </h3>
</div>
<div id="elementor-tab-content-2027"><p>Yes — and integrating lawn and garden elements from a single design team produces significantly better results than combining services from separate companies. When lawn areas, planting beds, irrigation zones, and garden features are all designed together, they work as a system — irrigation is sized correctly for both turf and planting, transitions between lawn and beds are designed cleanly, and the overall landscape has visual cohesion that’s hard to achieve when different companies are working from separate plans.</p>
</div>

<div id="do-you-cross-link-your-brighton-landscape-work-with-services-in-other-denver-metro-cities"><h3>Do you cross-link your Brighton landscape work with services in other Denver metro cities?</h3>
</div>
<div id="elementor-tab-content-2028"><p>Yes. Ridgewell serves the broader Denver metro area including Arvada, Aurora, Lakewood, and Brighton. If you’ve found us through a search for landscaping services in Brighton, we work across the region and bring the same team and standards to every city we serve. We’re happy to discuss projects anywhere in our service area during your initial consultation.</p>
</div>

